{"name":"Garrison Grey","hex":"#7b8588","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garrison","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A permanent military post.","The troops stationed at such a post."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To assign troops to a military post.","To convert into a military fort."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garrison"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garrison","blocks":[{"text":"A garrison is a body of troops stationed in a particular location, originally to guard it and the facilities that constitute a military base or fortified military headquarters. A garrison is usually in a city, town, fort, castle, ship, or similar site. \"Garrison town\" is a common expression for any town that has a military base nearby."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Siege_of_malta_1.jpg/330px-Siege_of_malta_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garrison","wikidata":"Q88556"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat.jpg/330px-Grey_Longhaired_Female_Cat